{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>When you come to the land of your habitations.</b> This passage is juxtaposed because they were weakened and mourned; to comfort the children, to inform them that they will come to the land. And the correct reason: because the entire congregation raised their voice (and sinned) and it was forgiven them through Moses' prayer, he said, \"And if you err,\" as a witness that it was forgiven them. And it was necessary to state the law of meal-offerings for every burnt-offering and sacrifice. And at the end, \"and the soul that acts with a high hand\" alludes to their deeds. And he mentioned the matter of the gatherer, because he acted with a high hand. And because of HaShem's abundant compassion for Israel, He appointed the fringes as a remembrance, so that a person will not act with a high hand, or so that he will not forget."], :book :numbers, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:17:46.216065523Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}